A||||6||photo-man|| v8 starter/flexplate set-up for auto trans?||||1||
Z||000000||photo-man||08-22-2000||07:39 PM||||my v8 chevy is now finished being built. i have not decided on which "kit" style to go with and how much of "kit" i really need. i need to know what starter and flexplate to get or do i have to get the one according to the style of trans/engine adapter used?<BR>any other suppliers of adapter plates other than v8archies or is my best source of supplies? and i almost forgot...ant alternative sources for front engine mounts?<BR>what you v8 guys use?<BR>many thanks!!!<BR>(86gt fastback) ||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||08-22-2000||10:47 PM||||We'll my kit I use was the Archie Deluxe Kit. The middle of the three kits. I bought this one cause it came with the starter and the water pump system. The starter must have three different mount positions on the mounting block. The flexplate I used was the stock 4cyl. The 6 cyl wont work cause of balancing. The rest of the parts to finish the install is pretty staight forward. Bolts, exhaust, hoses. etc.<P> Good luck on your install....<P>Scooter||||reg||1
Z||000002||ourufo||08-23-2000||07:17 AM||||If you buy a basic kit, make shure a parts store is close to you. You Will be going there often..<BR> OH YA! bring donuts and coffie.lol<P>------------------<BR>OURUFOV8||||reg||12
Z||000003||Lou Christopher||08-23-2000||12:18 PM|||| I have a fiero with the archie kit, recent puchase. the 4 cyl flex plate, is 142 tooth unit.  Starters used are for 153 tooth chev flywheels.  Will work sort of but cause excessive wear. I have not found a starter that will fit and is designed for 142 tooth.  The 153 units have a pinion with 9 teeth, the 168 units have a pinion with 11 teeth. It seems that for 142 teeth you should have 7 or 8 teeth on the pinion.  If you find something good please let me know.  Water pump drive system is not acceptable.  I replaced it with a messier electric pump.  Alternator bracket does not allow removal of #1 plug without moving the alt. Needs modification. My next job.||||reg||1
Z||000004||elfiero||08-23-2000||04:30 PM||||I used a gear reduction starter but,I had to<BR>fabricate an adapter that bolts to the engine<BR>to trans adapter plate.If you look at all of<BR>archies pics,he is either a poor photog,or he<BR>makes it just blurry enough so you cant copy<BR>it!the flexplate is the 142T with a new<BR>center welded in.for waterpump drive,I revamped the stock surpentine drive-it works<BR>well.||||reg||6
Z||000005||rprevo||08-24-2000||04:12 PM|||| I modified my 4 cyl flywheel to bolt to the<BR>externaly balanced smallblock chevy.<BR>I was concerned about the number of teeth<BR>that the flywheel had but then I counted the<BR>number of teeth on my stock 4 cyl starter.<BR>then I checked the diameter of it.  My small<BR>block chevy starter and Iron duke starter<BR>had the same gears in it.<BR>In my oppinion if your seeing wear in the<BR>teeth somthing is not lined up correctly.<BR>I mounted my starter to the side of my<BR>engine block with a bracket that I made on a<BR>mill at work. I made my whole kit from scratch. But if you lack the skill or time<BR>to make the kit I think Archie has the most<BR>user friendly kit.<BR>  <BR>  Ray<BR>||||reg||1
